A [[Gender|male]] [[Rodian]] was a '''prisoner''' of a [[Tusken Raider]] tribe on the [[planet]] [[Tatooine]] around [[4 ABY]]. The prisoner was joined by another captive named [[Boba Fett]], a famed [[bounty hunter]]. When Fett attempted to escape, the Rodian alerted [[Unidentified Tusken Raider tribe|the Tusken Raiders]]. The two prisoners were then taken to collect [[water]] with a [[Unidentified Tusken Raider youngling|Tusken child]]. After finding a [[moisture farm]] being raided, the child had the prisoners dig for water pouches. That was when the Rodian stumbled upon a [[sand beast]] which attacked them and suffocated them in the sand.

==Biography==
{{Quote|Rodian. Do you want me to cut your bonds?|Boba Fett offers to free the Rodian|<ref name="Chapter 1" />}}
[[File:BobaRodianMassiffGuard-BoBFCh1.png|thumb|left|300px|The Rodian was taken prisoner by a tribe of Tuskens who also captured Boba Fett.]]
Around [[4 ABY]],<ref name="Date" /> a [[Rodian]] was a prisoner of a [[Tusken Raider]] tribe, which tied them up against a broken [[tree]] branch. The raiders took another captive,<ref name="Chapter 1" /> the famed [[bounty hunter]]<ref name="Boba Databank">{{Databank|boba-fett|Boba Fett}}</ref> [[Boba Fett]],<ref name="Chapter 1" /> who had been badly defeated in a [[Rescue of Han Solo|skirmish]] at a [[Great Pit of Carkoon|Sarlacc pit]].<ref name="RotJ">{{Film|VI}}</ref> Fett was tied up at a tree branch next to the Rodian by a [[fire]]place for the night, guarded by a [[Unidentified massiff|massiff]]. Waking up, the [[bounty]] [[Hunting|hunter]] looked around and exchanged a look with the Rodian prisoner, before breaking free of his bonds by baiting the [[massiff]] and using its [[Tooth|teeth]]. Fett then offered to free the Rodian, but they instead called out to the Tuskens, leading the freed prisoner to be pursued and quickly recaptured.<ref name="Chapter 1" />

The next morning, a [[Unidentified Tusken Raider youngling|Tusken child]] took the Rodian prisoner and Fett and led them across the dunes of Tatooine with the massiff, Fett stumbling due to how weak he had become. They arrived near a homestead which was being raided by a gang of [[Kajain'sa'Nikto]]s. The Tusken child instead led the Rodian and Fett to a separate place and told them to start digging for [[black melon]]s. While Fett could not understand the child's commands, the Rodian prisoner immediately began digging, leading their fellow captive to join them. The Rodian quickly found a [[Color|black]] melon and handed it to the Tusken before continuing to dig.<ref name="Chapter 1" />

[[File:SandCreatureKillsRodian-BoBFCh1.png|thumb|right|300px|A Tatooine sand beast kills the Rodian]]
As the two prisoners dug more, the Rodian found another black melon for the Tusken child, while Fett reluctantly handed over his first find. When the child and Massiff fell asleep, Fett complained to the Rodian, claiming they could escape, reach the settlement [[Anchorhead]] and get offworld. The Rodian ignored him, so he threatened to strangle him with his ankle chain, leading the Rodian to snap back at him until he advised him to lower his voice. Still digging, the Rodian then discovered a scaly [[limb]], which attacked him. A [[sand beast]] revealed itself from the sand and mauled the Rodian, [[Death|suffocating]] the prisoner in sand. Fett killed the creature after, and returned to the Tusken tribe with the child and Massiff.<ref name="Chapter 1" />

==Personality and traits==
The Rodian had [[Color|pink]] skin and black [[eye]]s. Despite being captive to the Tuskens, the prisoner was loyal to them, informing them of Fett's escape attempt and working willingly for the Tusken child. The Rodian only spoke and understood his [[Rodian (language)|native language]], being unable to understand Boba Fett in Galactic Basic Standard, who intended to free him by mistaking him for flaying him. Still, he did understand from the tone of voice when he was being insulted in the Galactic Basic Standard.<ref name="Chapter 1" />

==Equipment==
The Rodian wore a yellow and dark brown [[jumpsuit]] with brown [[boot]]s.<ref name="Chapter 1" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|[&hellip;] the Rodian prisoner is voiced by my good buddy, mega-talent @SamWitwer|Sound editor [[David W. Collins]]|<ref name="Sam Witwer">{{Twitter|DavidWCollins|status/1476318763788083201|David W. Collins|quote=the Rodian prisoner is voiced by my good buddy, mega-talent @SamWitwer|archivedate=20211229223151}}</ref>}}
The Rodian appeared in the flashbacks of "[[Chapter 1: Stranger in a Strange Land]]," the first episode of the [[Disney+]] series ''[[Star Wars: The Book of Boba Fett]]'', which was directed by [[Robert Rodriguez]]<ref name="Chapter 1" /> and released on [[December 29]], [[2021]].<ref name="Disney+">{{DisneyPlusYouTube|t9Ca4ARSfqA|Next On Disney+ &#124; December 2021}}</ref> Credited only as "Rodian Prisoner," [[Dawn Dininger]] provided visual portrayal<ref name="Chapter 1" /> and [[Sam Witwer]] voiced the character.<ref name="Sam Witwer" />

